        "original_id": "211f5bef-f380-5885-a589-2eee643e6a9a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Quesnelia, honeysuckle, Billbergiopsis\n- Taxonomy: genus, subgenus, species counts, synonymy\n- Places: eastern Brazil\n\nFacts:\n- Quesnelia is a plant genus endemic to eastern Brazil.\n- Quesnelia contains 22 known species.\n- Billbergiopsis is a subgenus of the genus Quesnelia.\n- Billbergiopsis contains 15 of the 20 described species of Quesnelia.\n- Honeysuckle refers to plants in the genus Lonicera.\n- Approximately 180 species of honeysuckle have been identified.\n- Honeysuckle is named for the edible sweet nectar obtainable from its tubular flowers.",
